1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
This is the starting point on our dummy YouTube account.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
And this is the dummy Bluesky feed before curation.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Recommendation feeds learn us for years,
then new accounts make us start over.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Curate turns what you want into a portable Passport
that works across platforms.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
You can ask naturally: less ragebait,
more science-based pages.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Or give an exact mix across astronomy, coding,
drawing, anime, and fragrance.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Paste a few YouTube and Bluesky links.
Descriptions are optional.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The agent reads the sample, turns the request into a plan,
and tests it in a bounded practice feed.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Curate measures the shift instead of stopping
at a list of suggested actions.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Here is the YouTube feed after the change.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
And here is Bluesky after the same intent was translated.

12
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Copy Feed carries the useful parts of your taste
from one app to another.

13
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Curate shows what transfers cleanly,
what needs another route, and how to roll back.

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Incognito creates a temporary feed for a conference,
trip, or deep-work session.

15
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
It expires automatically, or you can close it immediately
without changing your normal feed.

16
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Blend creates a shared view from selected tastes
without merging accounts.

17
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Natural language in, a feed that feels like yours out,
and a way back.
